## Analysis

**Validated modulus results (with reliable fits):**
| Experiment | polymer_wt | mixing_temp | bath_temp | pullcast_speed | N₂ | wait_time | nips_time | Modulus (MPa) | CV |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 17p5, 65°C, 10°C, 6mm/s, N₂, 15s, 1800s | 17.5 | 65 | 10 | 6 | T | 15 | 1800 | **708.9** | 0.129 |
| 18p5, 25°C, 5°C, 19mm/s, NoN₂, 330s, 1800s | 18.5 | 25 | 5 | 19 | F | 330 | 1800 | **667.1** | nan |
| 17p5, 55°C, 25°C, 11mm/s, N₂, 375s, 1300s | 17.5 | 55 | 25 | 11 | T | 375 | 1300 | **591.7** | 0.109 |
| 17, 35°C, 5°C, 8mm/s, N₂, 0s, 1200s | 17.0 | 35 | 5 | 8 | T | 0 | 1200 | **569.3** | 0.046 |
| 17, 25°C, 5°C, 10mm/s, N₂, 30s, 1200s | 17.0 | 25 | 5 | 10 | T | 30 | 1200 | **547.2** | 0.112 |

**Key observations:**
- Best validated modulus: 708.9 MPa at (17.5 wt%, 65°C, bath 10°C, 6 mm/s, N₂, 15s wait, 1800s)
- This candidate has only one independent measurement (run1 = 708.9; run2 = 474.7 — these are two independent syntheses at the same conditions, so this IS an independent repeat)
- Run1: 708.9 MPa; Run2: 474.7 MPa — large discrepancy (~33%), suggesting high synthesis variability at these conditions
- The 667.1 MPa result (18.5 wt%, 25°C, bath 5°C, 19mm/s, NoN₂, 330s) has no CV and poor fit quality (37/100), so it's less reliable
- Many experiments yield no modulus (all fits discarded)

**Explore mode — sparse regions:**
- High polymer_wt (19-21) with low bath_temp (5°C) and N₂ and moderate-high mixing_temp: mostly failed fits
- bath_temp = 5°C with polymer_wt ~18-19, N₂, short wait, high mixing_temp is underexplored with good results
- mixing_temp in 25-35°C range with bath_temp 5°C and polymer_wt ~18-19 has sparse coverage
- nips_bath_wait_time near 1800s with bath_temp 5°C and polymer_wt ~18 is underexplored
- pullcast_speed ~4 mm/s is not yet sampled
- polymer_wt ~18 with bath_temp 5°C, N₂, short wait, moderate mixing_temp is sparse

**Deliberate exploration target:**
- polymer_wt = 18.0 (moderate, good film formation history)
- mixing_temp = 45°C (between 35 and 55, undersampled in this polymer_wt range)
- bath_temp = 5°C (cold bath associated with higher moduli)
- pullcast_speed = 4 mm/s (not yet sampled)
- nitrogen = True (associated with better moduli)
- coupon_to_bath_wait_time = 180s (not yet sampled, between 120 and 225)
- nips_bath_wait_time = 1800s (max, associated with best result)

This combination is genuinely novel — no near-duplicate exists in the dataset.

