## Explore Mode Analysis

The best validated result is 17.5wt%/65°C/6mm/s/N2/15s/10°C/1800s (708.9 MPa), but it has no independent repeat yet. However, the mode is **explore** — I should target sparse/underrepresented regions.

**Sparse regions identified:**
- `mixing_temp` ~25–35°C with `polymer_wt` ~18–19wt% and `bath_temp` ~5°C is somewhat covered, but `mixing_temp` ~25°C + `polymer_wt` ~19wt% + low wait time + N2 + cold bath is not explored
- `bath_temp` = 5°C is heavily sampled; bath_temp values of 5, 10, 15, 20, 25 are covered but combinations with higher polymer_wt (~19–20wt%) + high mixing_temp + short wait + N2 + bath_temp=5 are sparse
- `nips_bath_wait_time` near 1200s with `polymer_wt` ~19–20wt% and `mixing_temp` ~50–70°C is underexplored
- `pullcast_speed` ~16–20mm/s with N2=True is sparse (most fast speeds used NoN2 or different conditions)
- `coupon_to_bath_wait_time` near 0s with higher polymer_wt (19–20wt%) and moderate mixing_temp is sparse

