**Key observations:**
- Best single measurement: 709 MPa (17.5wt%, 65°C mix, 10°C bath, 6mm/s, N2, 15s, 1800s) — but run2 gave only 475 MPa with poor fit quality. This candidate has been repeated but the repeat shows a large discrepancy, suggesting the 709 value may not be reliably reproducible. No further validation is needed per policy since an independent repeat exists.
- Second-best reliable: 667 MPa (18.5wt%, 25°C mix, 5°C bath, 19mm/s, no N2, 330s, 1800s) — single measurement, no CV, 3 discarded fits. Uncertain.
- 596 MPa (18wt%, 45°C mix, 5°C bath, 4mm/s, N2, 180s, 1800s) — no CV, 3 discarded.
- 592 MPa (17.5wt%, 55°C mix, 25°C bath, 11mm/s, N2, 375s, 1300s) — reasonable.

**Explore mode — sparse regions:**
Looking at coverage:
- `bath_temp`: 5 values used (5, 10, 15, 20, 25°C) — all 5 levels covered but bath_temp=5°C is heavily sampled
- `mixing_temp`: 25–80°C covered but mid-range (around 50°C) with bath_temp combinations is sparse
- `polymer_wt`: 17–21 covered; 17–17.5 range is dense; 18–19 range has some coverage; higher wt% (20–21) sparse with good conditions
- `nips_bath_wait_time`: 1200–1800s, mostly at extremes; mid-range 1200–1500 less explored with N2+low bath temp
- `coupon_to_bath_wait_time`: 0–600s well covered; very short times (0–30s) with specific combos sparse

**Underrepresented region:** High polymer_wt (~20–21wt%) combined with low bath_temp (5°C), moderate mixing_temp (~35–40°C), moderate-high pullcast speed, N2, short wait time, and mid nips_bath_wait_time. The 21wt% experiment failed (poor membrane). 20wt% at 45°C/5°C bath/7mm/s/N2/150s/1650s had no modulus (all fits failed). 20.5wt% at 50°C/5°C/5mm/s/no N2/225s/1750s also no modulus.

